[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a one-line edit, but it changes a security boundary, so I want a yes before I touch it.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m — [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js[39m reads it directly as the session expiry.

  Consequence: a stolen or abandoned session stays valid for 8 hours instead of 30 minutes — a 16x wider window for
  session hijacking, and on shared or unattended machines a walked-away session stays logged in for a full workday.
  Whether that's acceptable depends on what these sessions authorize, which I can't see from this repo.
